president could make peace with China. Maybe only Trump can go to Tehran.

01:29:39.360 --> 01:29:48.000
Okay. But his, let me let me ask you a follow up on that. He keeps saying he wants Iran to do a

01:29:48.000 --> 01:29:56.800
deal, but really he wants Iran to surrender to his terms. And his terms are absolutely unacceptable.

01:29:56.800 --> 01:29:59.840
They're not even his. They're Benjamin Netanyahu's terms.

01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:05.160
But including the missiles, you can't give up the missiles if you're a sovereign nation

01:30:05.160 --> 01:30:07.560
because then you would be destroyed.

01:30:07.560 --> 01:30:12.040
So how does Trump expect anyone to agree to these terms?

01:30:12.040 --> 01:30:17.080
This is literally the one thing about Donald Trump that I just simply don't understand.

01:30:17.080 --> 01:30:22.520
I don't understand why he is so susceptible to pressure from Benjamin Netanyahu.

01:30:22.520 --> 01:30:23.680
You're exactly right.

01:30:23.680 --> 01:30:25.800
The Israeli government demands are clear.

01:30:25.800 --> 01:30:34.640
They've made them public and that is no uranium enrichment period, no ballistic missiles period.

01:30:34.640 --> 01:30:35.640
And you're right.

01:30:35.640 --> 01:30:39.960
You cease to be a country if you can't defend yourself and can't have a missile system.

01:30:39.960 --> 01:30:41.640
So what is that?

01:30:41.640 --> 01:30:49.720
The Israelis have also talked increasingly less discreetly about the end goal being

01:30:49.720 --> 01:30:53.080
to divide Iran up into five small countries.

01:30:53.080 --> 01:31:00.920
There would be Balochistan, Arabistan, Kurdistan, you know, five little rump countries because

01:31:00.920 --> 01:31:03.240
then they're much more easily controlled.

01:31:03.240 --> 01:31:06.320
The Israelis have good relations with Azerbaijan, for example.

01:31:06.320 --> 01:31:10.920
They have a base in Azerbaijan from which they can attack Iran.

01:31:10.920 --> 01:31:15.240
They have good relations with Iran and Iraq's Kurds.

01:31:15.240 --> 01:31:19.960
They're funding the Mujahideen-e-Khalq, the MEK terrorist group that we're now

01:31:19.960 --> 01:31:21.360
in bed with.

01:31:21.360 --> 01:31:27.560
So I think that this end goal of the Israelis to carve up Iran into five different countries

01:31:27.560 --> 01:31:32.440
is what they're going to try to eventually get Donald Trump to do.

01:31:32.440 --> 01:31:37.000
And this is nothing but catastrophe for all of us.

01:31:37.000 --> 01:31:38.440
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:31:38.440 --> 01:31:40.960
That makes sense to me what you just said there.

01:31:40.960 --> 01:31:43.960
So let me add this question into it.

01:31:43.960 --> 01:31:53.240
Is it possible that Trump and the DOD are fantastically underestimating the increased weapons potential

01:31:53.240 --> 01:32:00.680
of Iran even since last June because of technology shipments from both China and Texas from Russia?

01:32:00.680 --> 01:32:01.680
Exactly.

01:32:01.680 --> 01:32:07.880
Plus, Iran's own domestic engineering capabilities, which are significant and very smart engineers

01:32:07.880 --> 01:32:09.760
and mathematicians, right?

01:32:09.760 --> 01:32:13.240
So it seems to me like I'm hearing from Trump and I'm hearing from the MAGA people

01:32:13.240 --> 01:32:15.360
like, yeah, America, we're the best.

01:32:15.360 --> 01:32:16.360
We're undefeatable.

01:32:16.360 --> 01:32:20.640
And I'm starting to think like, well, what about the laws of physics?

01:32:20.640 --> 01:32:26.760
You know, hypersonic missiles, ballistic missiles, anti-ship missiles, et cetera.

01:32:26.760 --> 01:32:27.760
Where do you even start?

01:32:27.760 --> 01:32:28.760
Right.

01:32:28.760 --> 01:32:29.760
Hypersonic missiles.

01:32:29.760 --> 01:32:30.760
We don't have hypersonics yet.

01:32:30.760 --> 01:32:33.600
We're experimenting with them, but we don't have hypersonics yet.

01:32:33.600 --> 01:32:34.600
The Iranians do.

01:32:34.600 --> 01:32:35.600
They've tested them.

01:32:35.600 --> 01:32:36.600
Number one.

01:32:36.600 --> 01:32:37.600
Right.

01:32:37.600 --> 01:32:45.160
You remember prior to the 12-day war, the Israelis bombed Iran, and the Iranians responded with

01:32:45.160 --> 01:32:48.080
something like 600 drones.

01:32:48.080 --> 01:32:52.760
These were slow-motion drones called suicide drones, so they're not going to come back.

01:32:52.760 --> 01:32:55.280
They just crash into whatever the target is.

01:32:55.280 --> 01:33:01.080
They warned the Israelis in advance that the drones were coming, and they did that

01:33:01.080 --> 01:33:03.320
just because they had to save face domestically.

01:33:03.320 --> 01:33:06.640
Like, well, the Israelis attacked us, so now we're going to attack them with

01:33:06.640 --> 01:33:08.640
these drones.

01:33:08.640 --> 01:33:12.080
They warned the Israelis through the Jordanians that the drones were coming.

01:33:12.080 --> 01:33:18.600
All the drones were shot down, but seven out of, I think it was 600.

01:33:18.600 --> 01:33:24.240
That's actually valuable intelligence, that the Israeli Iron Dome is not perfect and

01:33:24.240 --> 01:33:32.360
seven slow-motion drones that you have watched for the past six hours try to make their

01:33:32.360 --> 01:33:37.600
way across Iraq and across Jordan, and you still couldn't shoot it down.

01:33:37.600 --> 01:33:40.680
And shooting down the other drones costs a billion dollars or something.

01:33:40.680 --> 01:33:42.120
And that was my second point.

01:33:42.120 --> 01:33:43.120
Right.

01:33:43.120 --> 01:33:47.920
The reason why that war only lasted 12 days was because the Israelis ran out of missiles.

01:33:47.920 --> 01:33:48.920
Right.

01:33:48.920 --> 01:33:49.920
They're just out.

01:33:49.920 --> 01:33:51.240
They used them all.

01:33:51.240 --> 01:33:53.780
And have they had a chance to replenish them?

01:33:53.780 --> 01:33:57.040
We don't know, but a lot of observers say no.

01:33:57.040 --> 01:34:04.800
In the meantime, you've made an important point that sanctions, which have gone on for 47 years

01:34:04.800 --> 01:34:11.660
now, have forced the Iranians to fend for themselves, right?

01:34:11.660 --> 01:34:16.680
So if they have a need for something that they can't buy because of sanctions, they

01:34:16.680 --> 01:34:20.880
just make it themselves, and they've become quite good at it.

01:34:20.880 --> 01:34:27.240
All that with the technology that they are able to procure from China and Russia, and

01:34:27.240 --> 01:34:30.600
the Iranians want for nothing.

01:34:30.600 --> 01:34:32.400
They're prepared for the Israelis.

01:34:32.400 --> 01:34:39.800
Also, Iran is a country of 92 million people, and it's the size of Germany.

01:34:39.800 --> 01:34:42.480
This is a major country we're talking about.

01:34:42.480 --> 01:34:45.680
It's not just going to collapse because you fire a rocket at it.

01:34:45.680 --> 01:34:46.680
That's right.

01:34:46.680 --> 01:34:48.160
You're going to have to commit ground troops.

01:34:48.160 --> 01:34:51.280
And I don't think that as a country, we have the stomach for something like that.

01:34:51.280 --> 01:34:54.280
Well, let me go back to something you just said.

01:34:54.280 --> 01:35:00.340
You're really talking about the economic asymmetry of how Iran can launch low cost

01:35:00.340 --> 01:35:04.880
drones that require Israel to defend with extremely high cost interceptors.

01:35:04.880 --> 01:35:09.400
But I want to add another element to this and ask you about your knowledge on this.

01:35:09.400 --> 01:35:14.680
The interceptors, which are mostly manufactured by U.S. weapons companies, they rely,

01:35:14.680 --> 01:35:20.560
of course, very heavily on these so-called rare earths that China has slapped major export

01:35:20.560 --> 01:35:26.120
restrictions on, including everything from gallium and dysprosium and neodymium and magnets

01:35:26.120 --> 01:35:28.360
and guidance and radar systems.

01:35:28.360 --> 01:35:32.200
And all of these elements are extremely highly restricted.

01:35:32.200 --> 01:35:36.320
Now, there's been a pass on some of those elements until the end of this year, but

01:35:36.320 --> 01:35:42.080
China could revoke that pass at any time in addition to selling off U.S. treasuries

01:35:42.080 --> 01:35:43.320
and whatever else.

01:35:43.480 --> 01:35:45.480
So China has a lot of cards to play.

01:35:45.480 --> 01:35:50.520
If the U.S. attacks Iran, wouldn't China say, well, we can't let Iran fall because it's

01:35:50.520 --> 01:35:54.880
the gateway between the East and the Middle and Africa and Europe and everything?

01:35:55.480 --> 01:36:02.000
So we're just going to use economic weapons and resource weapons of restrictions

01:36:02.000 --> 01:36:02.840
against the United States.

01:36:02.840 --> 01:36:06.400
And then the U.S. won't be able to build the interceptors to give to Israel

01:36:06.400 --> 01:36:08.600
to defend itself against Iran.

01:36:08.600 --> 01:36:09.360
Does that make sense?

01:36:09.360 --> 01:36:11.120
You see, that makes perfect sense.

01:36:11.160 --> 01:36:15.960
It's not just a question of, oh, should we hit them or should we not hit them?

01:36:16.440 --> 01:36:18.760
There are an awful lot of moving parts in this.

01:36:18.920 --> 01:36:21.960
And one of the things that the Chinese saw early on was the value,

01:36:21.960 --> 01:36:24.040
the import of rare earth metals.

01:36:24.240 --> 01:36:30.200
We were getting most of our rare earth metals from the Congo when that was a country.

01:36:31.040 --> 01:36:33.240
They're just flush with rare earth metals.

01:36:33.520 --> 01:36:36.640
But the problem with rare earths, they exist all over the place.

01:36:36.640 --> 01:36:40.040
We even have them under the Salton Sea in the California desert.

01:36:40.320 --> 01:36:45.480
They're very, very expensive to mine because most of what you mine with rare

01:36:45.480 --> 01:36:46.760
earths is just waste.

01:36:46.760 --> 01:36:49.280
It's rock and sand and it's just wasted.

01:36:49.520 --> 01:36:55.560
So it costs you more to mine it than the value of the finished ore.

01:36:56.400 --> 01:37:01.440
Well, the Chinese are willing to take that economic loss because first,

01:37:01.440 --> 01:37:03.920
their economy is very robust and they have the money.

01:37:04.280 --> 01:37:09.640
They spend literally a fraction, less than a 10 percent of what

01:37:09.640 --> 01:37:14.120
we spend on national defense or about 10 percent of what we spend on national

01:37:14.120 --> 01:37:21.520
defense and it allows them to control the entire world market for rare earth metals.

01:37:22.240 --> 01:37:29.080
So what happens then, as you just posed, when we attack Iran on behalf of Israel,

01:37:29.080 --> 01:37:30.840
we fight Israel's battle for it.

01:37:31.600 --> 01:37:36.120
And then the Chinese cut us off from the sale of rare earth metals.

01:37:36.400 --> 01:37:38.720
What are we going to use for missile guidance systems?

01:37:38.960 --> 01:37:42.680
Or cell phones or the computers that run our cars?

01:37:43.160 --> 01:37:45.360
You made a second point that I think bears repeating.

01:37:46.720 --> 01:37:49.520
The Chinese are, depending on what numbers you're looking at,

01:37:49.520 --> 01:37:55.960
the second or third largest holder of long term government treasury bonds.

01:37:56.920 --> 01:38:00.960
If the Chinese really want to put the pain to us,

01:38:01.600 --> 01:38:06.000
they can just dump those bonds and our entire economy would crash.

01:38:06.840 --> 01:38:08.800
So, you know, is it really worth it?

01:38:08.800 --> 01:38:11.080
Do we really want to do this?

01:38:11.080 --> 01:38:14.560
Besides the fact that you're probably not going to get your Nobel Peace Prize

01:38:14.560 --> 01:38:16.440
for waging a war of choice.

01:38:16.440 --> 01:38:20.680
But see these these repercussions that you mentioned, these are costs

01:38:20.680 --> 01:38:23.280
to America, but not costs to Netanyahu.

01:38:23.280 --> 01:38:27.160
So from Netanyahu's point of view, he doesn't care if he throws

01:38:27.160 --> 01:38:31.080
America under the bus or if America bleeds out economically, right?

01:38:31.160 --> 01:38:36.520
As long as Israel gets what he wants, which is chaos in the Middle East.

01:38:37.520 --> 01:38:40.480
See, but you can't say that out loud because then you're an anti-Semite.

01:38:41.120 --> 01:38:43.880
You know, I said exactly the same thing a few weeks ago.

01:38:43.880 --> 01:38:47.080
And the Israeli Foreign Minister's political director wrote an article

01:38:47.080 --> 01:38:49.760
saying that I was a noted anti-Semite.

01:38:50.160 --> 01:38:51.120
And I was like, what?

01:38:51.120 --> 01:38:53.760
Well, the but the word is lost all meaning now.

01:38:53.760 --> 01:38:56.680
Yes, it has just like sanctions, you know,

01:38:56.720 --> 01:39:00.960
sanctions sort of sort of forced the the Iranians to stand on their

01:39:00.960 --> 01:39:05.760
own or their own two feet, calling everybody who disagrees with one

01:39:05.760 --> 01:39:08.960
of your policies in anti-Semite has made the meaning worthless.

01:39:09.120 --> 01:39:10.600
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

01:39:10.600 --> 01:39:12.760
And also sanctions didn't work against Russia.

01:39:12.760 --> 01:39:15.040
It just made Russia's domestic industry stronger.

01:39:16.120 --> 01:39:18.640
Well, Foreign Minister Lavrov said two things.

01:39:18.640 --> 01:39:22.480
He said, number one, the Russians were surprised at the swiftness

01:39:22.480 --> 01:39:24.640
with which the Americans implemented sanctions.

01:39:24.680 --> 01:39:27.520
He said that just a week after the sanctions were announced.

01:39:27.840 --> 01:39:31.800
And then a year or two later, he said he was surprised at the quickness

01:39:31.960 --> 01:39:34.640
with which the Russians were able to get around sanctions.

01:39:35.280 --> 01:39:36.680
Let me add one other thing.

01:39:36.680 --> 01:39:39.640
I went to China last year on a business trip.

01:39:39.640 --> 01:39:41.480
It's the first time I had ever been to China.

01:39:42.200 --> 01:39:47.200
And I had trouble finding places that would take a visa or a master card.

01:39:47.520 --> 01:39:50.640
But everybody took this thing called the octopus card.

01:39:51.280 --> 01:39:53.200
So finally, I asked one of the shopkeepers,

01:39:53.200 --> 01:39:55.960
what is this octopus card I keep seeing everywhere?

01:39:56.160 --> 01:39:59.400
He said, oh, that's that's kind of our national credit card of China.

01:39:59.640 --> 01:39:59.960
I said.

01:40:00.000 --> 01:40:02.480
Why don't you just use MasterCard and Visa?

01:40:02.480 --> 01:40:05.040
And he said, because MasterCard and Visa

01:40:05.040 --> 01:40:07.760
put every transaction through New York,

01:40:07.760 --> 01:40:12.000
which makes it susceptible to American sanctions.

01:40:12.000 --> 01:40:14.560
He said, octopus card goes through Shanghai.

01:40:14.560 --> 01:40:17.120
So we don't have to worry about American sanctions.

01:40:17.120 --> 01:40:19.880
And that is what happens when you overuse

01:40:19.880 --> 01:40:21.680
and overimpose sanctions.

01:40:21.680 --> 01:40:23.360
Yes, yes.

01:40:23.360 --> 01:40:25.400
Okay, now speaking of China,

01:40:25.400 --> 01:40:28.800
we've all seen China shipping many cargo planes

01:40:28.800 --> 01:40:31.200
