they should have developed it 20 years ago,

01:45:02.360 --> 01:45:03.440
it should be out today.

01:45:03.440 --> 01:45:05.640
And it should be Star Trek kind of stuff.

01:45:05.640 --> 01:45:06.880
And it's not.

01:45:06.880 --> 01:45:07.720
It's not.

01:45:07.720 --> 01:45:09.720
You know, we've been told for decades

01:45:09.720 --> 01:45:11.240
they're working on this robot.

01:45:11.240 --> 01:45:13.640
It's gonna make soldiers obsolete.

01:45:13.640 --> 01:45:15.440
They just need to figure out the battery.

01:45:15.440 --> 01:45:16.600
Well, you know what?

01:45:16.640 --> 01:45:18.800
The South Koreans figured out the battery.

01:45:18.800 --> 01:45:20.880
And now South Korea,

01:45:20.880 --> 01:45:24.000
I should say Hyundai's a subsidiary in South Korea

01:45:24.000 --> 01:45:25.200
that builds robots.

01:45:25.200 --> 01:45:26.600
It was highlighted in the Wall Street Journal

01:45:26.600 --> 01:45:27.880
over the weekend.

01:45:27.880 --> 01:45:30.000
They're ready to go to market with their robots

01:45:30.000 --> 01:45:32.880
with long life batteries

01:45:32.880 --> 01:45:36.360
that can do things like get in a self-driving car

01:45:36.360 --> 01:45:38.000
and go do your grocery shopping.

01:45:38.000 --> 01:45:38.840
Yeah, yeah.

01:45:38.840 --> 01:45:40.160
How come we don't have that?

01:45:40.160 --> 01:45:41.000
Have you seen?

01:45:41.000 --> 01:45:42.880
Why hasn't DARPA figured that out?

01:45:42.880 --> 01:45:45.040
China, two of China's top companies,

01:45:45.040 --> 01:45:47.720
BYD and CATL, CATL, right?

01:45:47.720 --> 01:45:49.640
I mean, their battery technology

01:45:49.640 --> 01:45:51.080
is 20 years ahead of anything in AWS.

01:45:51.080 --> 01:45:51.920
State of the art.

01:45:51.920 --> 01:45:52.760
State of the art.

01:45:52.760 --> 01:45:54.160
When I went to China last year,

01:45:54.160 --> 01:45:58.440
I said to a member of our group

01:45:58.440 --> 01:45:59.680
who was from Hong Kong,

01:45:59.680 --> 01:46:00.920
she's an attorney.

01:46:00.920 --> 01:46:03.680
I said, what is this car, this BYD?

01:46:03.680 --> 01:46:05.880
She said, yeah, it stands for Beyond Your Dreams.

01:46:05.880 --> 01:46:07.200
It's our electric car.

01:46:07.200 --> 01:46:08.920
I said, this car is gorgeous.

01:46:08.920 --> 01:46:09.840
They're amazing.

01:46:09.840 --> 01:46:12.440
The design, it's just beautiful to look at.

01:46:12.440 --> 01:46:14.240
And she said, yeah, they're really cheap.

01:46:14.240 --> 01:46:16.200
They're gonna be the number one car

01:46:16.200 --> 01:46:17.920
in a lot of different countries around the world.

01:46:17.920 --> 01:46:19.760
And they're now number one in Canada,

01:46:19.760 --> 01:46:20.920
number one in Australia,

01:46:20.920 --> 01:46:23.240
number one in New Zealand.

01:46:23.240 --> 01:46:24.920
Sales are booming in Europe.

01:46:24.920 --> 01:46:27.480
I said, I've never heard of this car.

01:46:27.480 --> 01:46:29.120
We don't have these in the United States.

01:46:29.120 --> 01:46:32.680
And she said, because you guys banned them

01:46:32.680 --> 01:46:36.080
